WEBVTT

00:10.480 --> 00:16.200
<b><i>Yahiko is Kamiya Kasshin-ryu's
precious successor, that he is.</i></b>

01:54.000 --> 01:58.010
<b>EPISODE 14: YAHIKO'S BATTLE</b>

01:59.220 --> 02:00.470
<b>Yahiko is missing?</b>

02:00.680 --> 02:02.100
<b>Yes, he is!</b>

02:02.100 --> 02:06.230
<b>Come to think of it, he disappears
every so often lately, that he does.</b>

02:06.230 --> 02:07.060
<b>Doesn't he?</b>

02:07.270 --> 02:09.650
<b>Maybe he got a girl or somethin'.</b>

02:09.650 --> 02:11.690
<b>He's quite sassy, you know.</b>

02:12.020 --> 02:15.110
<b>I'm sure he's eating some snacks,
whether he bought them or found them!</b>

02:15.110 --> 02:17.070
<b>His greediness is full-fledged already!</b>

02:17.280 --> 02:21.700
<b>I think he is working hard on practicing
his swordsmanship by himself, that I do.</b>

02:21.990 --> 02:26.450
<b>He should be starting to see visions of
what his own swordsmanship is, that he is.</b>

02:26.700 --> 02:27.660
<b>- No way!
- No way!</b>

02:28.160 --> 02:29.670
<b>You think so?</b>

02:29.870 --> 02:32.290
<b>A girl. A girl! It's gotta be a girl!</b>

02:32.290 --> 02:35.460
<b>Food. It's got to be food.
There's no doubt about it!</b>

02:35.460 --> 02:36.710
<b>I think it's swordsmanship—</b>

02:36.710 --> 02:37.760
<b>- No way!
- No way!</b>

02:38.420 --> 02:39.260
<b>Food!</b>

02:39.380 --> 02:40.220
<b>A girl!</b>

02:40.720 --> 02:45.180
<b>What earthly nonsense are you two
blathering about? So pathetic.</b>

02:45.430 --> 02:46.600
<b>So cheeky!</b>

02:46.810 --> 02:47.770
<b>Sheesh!</b>

02:47.770 --> 02:48.770
<b>Gimme a break!</b>

02:50.310 --> 02:51.310
<b>What the...</b>

02:53.900 --> 02:56.570
<b>Where have you been,
that you have, Yahiko?</b>

02:57.480 --> 02:58.860
<b>Just out on a walk.</b>

02:59.570 --> 03:02.200
<b>Ditching your training
to go out on a stroll</b>

03:02.200 --> 03:04.370
<b>is not just a walk, that it isn't.</b>

03:06.450 --> 03:08.450
<b>I do my practice swings in the morning,</b>

03:08.450 --> 03:11.670
<b>and of the six training days a week,
I properly show up for four of them,</b>

03:11.670 --> 03:12.790
<b>so it's okay.</b>

03:13.080 --> 03:15.130
<b>It's nothing you should worry about.</b>

03:15.130 --> 03:15.960
<b>Oro...</b>

03:18.420 --> 03:19.550
<b>Hmm...</b>

03:20.510 --> 03:23.390
<b>AND A FEW DAYS LATER</b>

03:21.090 --> 03:26.390
<b>KAMIYA KASSHIN
SCHOOL OF KENDO</b>

03:29.100 --> 03:29.980
<b>All right.</b>

03:31.350 --> 03:34.560
<b>KAMIYA KASSHIN
SCHOOL OF KENDO</b>

03:34.810 --> 03:36.400
<b>He really is suspicious.</b>

03:36.400 --> 03:38.780
<b>He's hiding something, that he is.</b>

03:38.780 --> 03:41.530
<b>Well, this is a great way to kill time.</b>

03:43.990 --> 03:45.320
<b>A girl! It's a girl!</b>

03:45.320 --> 03:46.990
<b>Food! I said it's food!</b>

03:46.990 --> 03:49.700
<b>I think he's training his swordsmanship,
that I do.</b>

03:50.500 --> 03:54.040
<b>BEEF HOT-POT AND SAKE
AKABEKO RESTAURANT</b>

03:51.410 --> 03:54.040
<b>What the? We're at Akabeko.</b>

03:54.250 --> 03:57.170
<b>See? It really was food!</b>

03:57.170 --> 03:58.000
<b>Oro?</b>

03:59.340 --> 04:01.470
<b>Sneaking off to come here
on a regular basis...</b>

04:02.800 --> 04:05.050
<b>Wait, huh?</b>

04:05.260 --> 04:08.760
<b>That's strange.
I'm sure he came in here.</b>

04:08.760 --> 04:10.390
<b>Oh, Kaoru!</b>

04:10.600 --> 04:13.600
<b>Welcome! We have some open seats.</b>

04:13.600 --> 04:14.770
<b>Go ahead and sit down.</b>

04:15.020 --> 04:16.730
<b>Yeah, sorry to barge in.</b>

04:16.730 --> 04:18.320
<b>That's not it.</b>

04:18.320 --> 04:19.900
<b>Miss Tae, actually...</b>

04:22.240 --> 04:23.570
<b>Hey, boy!</b>

04:23.820 --> 04:27.030
<b>I don't have enough coal. Grab me a bag!</b>

04:27.030 --> 04:28.030
<b>Yeah!</b>

04:28.240 --> 04:30.160
<b>Tsubame, you go get a bag, too.</b>

04:30.160 --> 04:34.250
<b>It's getting crowded in there,
so when you're done, go over as a server!</b>

04:34.250 --> 04:35.500
<b>O-Okay.</b>

04:36.000 --> 04:37.000
<b>I see.</b>

04:37.750 --> 04:39.960
<b>So working as a day laborer, that he is.</b>

04:39.960 --> 04:42.340
<b>Actually, he told me
not to tell you about it.</b>

04:42.590 --> 04:46.800
<b>He came here and asked me to hire him,
but kept it a secret from you.</b>

04:47.010 --> 04:48.510
<b>Why would he do such a thing?</b>

04:49.470 --> 04:51.390
<b>Maybe that's what he's after?</b>

04:51.720 --> 04:52.600
<b>"That"?</b>

04:53.640 --> 04:55.440
<b>Oh, Tsubame?</b>

04:55.810 --> 04:57.520
<b>It wouldn't be her.</b>

04:57.520 --> 05:01.530
<b>Tsubame started working for us
after Yahiko did.</b>

05:01.730 --> 05:03.440
<b>What are you doing?</b>

05:03.440 --> 05:05.280
<b>I'm sorry, Little Yahiko.</b>

05:05.280 --> 05:07.360
<b>Stop saying I'm little!</b>

05:07.360 --> 05:08.240
<b>I'm sorry!</b>

05:11.830 --> 05:15.250
<b>Don't be so sobby and jittery.</b>

05:15.410 --> 05:18.500
<b>I hate people like that.</b>

05:18.630 --> 05:19.790
<b>Little Yah—</b>

05:19.790 --> 05:21.170
<b>Uh, Yahiko...</b>

05:21.170 --> 05:24.220
<b>Training my lower body
is part of swordsmanship training.</b>

05:24.220 --> 05:26.760
<b>So just hurry up, and go serve people.</b>

05:29.800 --> 05:32.850
<b>Food, a girl, and swordsmanship training.</b>

05:33.140 --> 05:35.560
<b>We have all three here, at least.</b>

05:35.770 --> 05:38.600
<b>But none of them are his real objective,
that they aren't.</b>

05:39.020 --> 05:41.400
<b>Does that mean he's just getting
a bit of pocket cash?</b>

05:41.520 --> 05:42.530
<b>If that's the case,</b>

05:42.530 --> 05:45.490
<b>why is he telling people to stay quiet
and hiding it from us?</b>

05:45.490 --> 05:46.450
<b>Hmm...</b>

05:46.650 --> 05:52.080
<b>Perhaps he is trying to help out
with the Kamiya Dojo's budget?</b>

05:52.200 --> 05:55.660
<b>Never! He doesn't have
that admirable a personality!</b>

05:55.660 --> 05:57.040
<b>Says you!</b>

05:57.040 --> 05:58.580
<b>You're eating on us without paying!</b>

05:58.580 --> 06:00.710
<b>Damn it! Our order's late!</b>

06:00.710 --> 06:02.290
<b>O-Okay, right away.</b>

06:02.960 --> 06:05.010
<b>Sorry for the wait. Your order—</b>

06:07.590 --> 06:08.630
<b>Hey.</b>

06:09.550 --> 06:12.010
<b>What's with that glum look on your face?</b>

06:12.220 --> 06:14.970
<b>Is that how you look at your master?</b>

06:17.390 --> 06:19.150
<b>Man, this is tough.</b>

06:19.690 --> 06:22.360
<b>This is tougher than Kaoru's training.</b>

06:22.860 --> 06:25.360
<b>But it's up to me
to make enough to get that.</b>

06:25.360 --> 06:26.990
<b>I can't complain about it.</b>

06:28.030 --> 06:31.120
<b>Come to think of it,
how much does that thing cost?</b>

06:31.620 --> 06:32.450
<b>Hmm?</b>

06:39.000 --> 06:41.040
<b>So, how was it?</b>

06:42.790 --> 06:44.750
<b>I'm asking you, how was it?</b>

06:46.460 --> 06:49.090
<b>Akabeko doesn't keep
a large stash of cash.</b>

06:49.090 --> 06:52.600
<b>The owner carries all profits
back home with him.</b>

06:52.850 --> 06:55.140
<b>Hmph. Just as I thought.</b>

06:56.100 --> 06:57.430
<b>Now give it to me.</b>

06:58.310 --> 07:00.520
<b>You made them
just like I told you to, right?</b>

07:00.730 --> 07:04.360
<b>The clay molds for the keys
to the owner's house and the warehouse!</b>

07:05.570 --> 07:08.530
<b>Y-You shouldn't be doing this, Lord Mikio!</b>

07:08.530 --> 07:09.740
<b>If you become a thief,</b>

07:09.740 --> 07:12.660
<b>you will tarnish the name of Nagaoka,
former vassal of the Shogun...</b>

07:13.160 --> 07:14.530
<b>Damn you.</b>

07:14.910 --> 07:18.370
<b>When have you had enough authority
to give me your opinions?</b>

07:18.660 --> 07:21.080
<b>You're nothing more
than the daughter of a poor samurai</b>

07:21.080 --> 07:25.590
<b>who survived by serving under my family
for the 300 years of Edo!</b>

07:25.920 --> 07:28.760
<b>And now that the revolution
changed how samurais live,</b>

07:28.760 --> 07:32.300
<b>my family and yours are strangers?</b>

07:32.550 --> 07:35.050
<b>Meiji really is a crummy time to live in!</b>

07:35.050 --> 07:37.390
<b>No loyalty to people or nothin'!</b>

07:37.600 --> 07:39.680
<b>Clamor for equality for the four classes,</b>

07:39.680 --> 07:43.600
<b>and you can trample on 300 years
of gratitude all you want!</b>

07:43.600 --> 07:46.610
<b>But... you really shouldn't steal.</b>

07:47.270 --> 07:52.320
<b>Oh, I get it. I won't ask
perfect strangers for anything.</b>

07:52.780 --> 07:55.570
<b>I'll do what I want from now on.</b>

07:55.870 --> 07:59.700
<b>Without a key, I gotta kill to steal,
but I have no choice.</b>

08:00.200 --> 08:04.290
<b>If there's a witness, I will tarnish
my cherished name of Nagaoka.</b>

08:05.000 --> 08:09.260
<b>Guess I'll have to kill everyone,
including that woman named Tae.</b>

08:13.180 --> 08:15.430
<b>Heh. That's how you should act.</b>

08:15.930 --> 08:17.050
<b>Are you an idiot?</b>

08:17.640 --> 08:20.180
<b>It's 10 years into Meiji already.</b>

08:20.180 --> 08:22.940
<b>Are you still trapped
in such a master-servant relationship?</b>

08:22.940 --> 08:23.770
<b>Who is it?</b>

08:23.770 --> 08:25.900
<b>Hey, Sideburns down there!</b>

08:25.900 --> 08:29.820
<b>As a fellow samurai,
I can't let you off the hook!</b>

08:29.980 --> 08:30.900
<b>Little Yahiko!</b>

08:31.030 --> 08:33.320
<b>I told you to cut the "little" stuff!</b>

08:37.620 --> 08:40.580
<b>Hey! Quit the stupid thoughts,
like stealing!</b>

08:40.830 --> 08:45.370
<b>If you don't, Tokyo samurai Yahiko Myojin
will take you on!</b>

08:45.370 --> 08:46.880
<b>You little brat!</b>

08:46.880 --> 08:48.000
<b>Don't be cheeky!</b>

08:48.000 --> 08:48.840
<b>Body!</b>

08:48.960 --> 08:50.050
<b>Damn you!</b>

08:51.670 --> 08:54.470
<b><i>I can do it!
My swordsmanship works well enough!</i></b>

08:54.470 --> 08:55.300
<b>Why, you...</b>

08:55.300 --> 08:56.140
<b>Come at me!</b>

08:58.760 --> 09:00.060
<b>Hey, give me that.</b>

09:03.980 --> 09:06.310
<b>Now! Surround and pummel him!</b>

09:09.440 --> 09:10.270
<b>Oro?</b>

09:10.520 --> 09:13.240
<b>Why are you so carefree,
posin' like you're just gonna watch?</b>

09:14.360 --> 09:16.860
<b>That's right! Yahiko is in trouble!</b>

09:17.070 --> 09:18.990
<b>Calm down, that you will.</b>

09:18.990 --> 09:20.780
<b>I can't stay calm!</b>

09:20.780 --> 09:23.330
<b>He is my precious first student!</b>

09:23.540 --> 09:24.790
<b>Hold on.</b>

09:25.000 --> 09:27.710
<b>Yahiko doesn't realize we are here.</b>

09:28.210 --> 09:31.500
<b>It's extremely unnatural for us
to show ourselves here, that it is.</b>

09:31.590 --> 09:32.420
<b>But—</b>

09:32.420 --> 09:36.720
<b>One never gets any stronger
if they are saved all the time.</b>

09:37.800 --> 09:39.640
<b>This is Yahiko's battle.</b>

09:40.140 --> 09:42.770
<b>It's one thing
if Yahiko is seeking us for help.</b>

09:43.060 --> 09:46.020
<b>This isn't something we should
be intruding upon, that it isn't.</b>

09:46.730 --> 09:52.440
<b><i>How they say lions send their cubs
down into the abyss of a ravine? But...</i></b>

09:53.730 --> 09:54.690
<b>Stop!</b>

09:54.860 --> 09:59.160
<b>Stop them, Lord Mikio!
He has nothing to do with it!</b>

09:59.160 --> 10:00.910
<b>I will give you the key molds!</b>

10:02.830 --> 10:06.750
<b>Hey! This is only a little taste
before the big event.</b>

10:06.750 --> 10:08.210
<b>That's enough.</b>

10:08.460 --> 10:09.330
<b>Yes, sir!</b>

10:11.750 --> 10:13.170
<b>A-Are you okay?</b>

10:13.670 --> 10:17.420
<b>Damn it, if I could go one-on-one,
those guys...</b>

10:17.420 --> 10:18.550
<b>Tsubame!</b>

10:19.300 --> 10:21.800
<b>Keep devoting yourself to me.</b>

10:22.890 --> 10:26.020
<b>See you, Little Yahiko.</b>

10:28.390 --> 10:31.940
<b>I'm sorry to get you
roped into all of this.</b>

10:33.020 --> 10:34.230
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

10:38.400 --> 10:43.240
<b>It will take at least one day
to make a precise key from a mold.</b>

10:43.660 --> 10:46.290
<b>They won't strike
until at least tomorrow night.</b>

10:46.290 --> 10:47.290
<b>Little Yahiko!</b>

10:47.910 --> 10:49.120
<b>I don't care.</b>

10:49.710 --> 10:53.590
<b>If I'm still losing to thugs like that,
I should be called "little."</b>

10:54.170 --> 10:59.180
<b>And I didn't get myself roped into this.
I decided to meddle in it myself.</b>

10:59.800 --> 11:02.140
<b>So you don't have to worry
about any of this.</b>

11:07.770 --> 11:09.100
<b>Little Yahiko...</b>

11:11.310 --> 11:13.310
<b><i>I can't talk to the cops.</i></b>

11:13.730 --> 11:15.820
<b><i>If I do, she'll become an accomplice.</i></b>

11:16.320 --> 11:18.780
<b><i>I can't rely on Kenshin or the others.</i></b>

11:19.400 --> 11:20.490
<b><i>More than anything else,</i></b>

11:20.490 --> 11:23.990
<b><i>I don't want to trouble them
with the likes of those guys.</i></b>

11:25.580 --> 11:28.540
<b><i>This is my battle!</i></b>

11:30.080 --> 11:33.080
<b>RUROUNI KENSHIN</b>

11:33.630 --> 11:36.340
<b>KAMIYA KASSHIN
SCHOOL OF KENDO</b>

11:33.630 --> 11:36.340
<b>NEXT MORNING</b>

11:37.420 --> 11:40.050
<b>I guess that about does it.</b>

11:40.340 --> 11:42.380
<b>What kind of toy is it?</b>

11:42.380 --> 11:47.140
<b>Idiot! This is an improvised training
machine to fight multiple enemies at once!</b>

11:47.350 --> 11:48.600
<b>You're so silly.</b>

11:49.020 --> 11:50.480
<b>Things like that are useless.</b>

11:50.680 --> 11:51.980
<b>What did you say?</b>

11:51.980 --> 11:53.190
<b>It's obvious.</b>

11:53.480 --> 11:57.070
<b>Those boards only move in a certain way,
but human swordsmanship doesn't.</b>

11:57.070 --> 11:59.320
<b>Coordination, waves, surrounding...</b>

11:59.690 --> 12:04.240
<b>all sorts of tactics
will be used for complicated attacks.</b>

12:05.160 --> 12:07.990
<b>Even if you were to train
just your reflexes,</b>

12:07.990 --> 12:09.790
<b>you can't do that in just a day.</b>

12:11.290 --> 12:13.000
<b>Call it a kid's shallow thinking.</b>

12:14.040 --> 12:15.000
<b>Shut up!</b>

12:18.000 --> 12:19.510
<b>Hey, Kenshin.</b>

12:19.630 --> 12:20.460
<b>Oro?</b>

12:20.710 --> 12:24.430
<b>You know anything
about how to fight multiple guys alone?</b>

12:24.930 --> 12:26.550
<b>What's this all of a sudden, that is?</b>

12:28.180 --> 12:30.640
<b>I just kinda wanna know.</b>

12:33.270 --> 12:34.100
<b>I see.</b>

12:34.940 --> 12:38.110
<b>There is one thing
I can think of, that I can.</b>

12:38.360 --> 12:39.400
<b>Really?</b>

12:39.400 --> 12:40.940
<b>Back in the Bakumatsu Era,</b>

12:40.940 --> 12:44.530
<b>Revolutionary warriors used this tactic
when they were hopelessly outnumbered.</b>

12:45.200 --> 12:47.240
<b>First of all, you run away, that you do.</b>

12:47.700 --> 12:48.530
<b>Run away?</b>

12:48.530 --> 12:49.370
<b>Right.</b>

12:50.450 --> 12:53.960
<b>To be precise,
you pretend to run away, that you do.</b>

12:54.670 --> 12:56.540
<b>Of course the enemy will come after you,</b>

12:56.540 --> 12:59.300
<b>but each man differs,
so their speeds will be inconsistent.</b>

12:59.300 --> 13:02.510
<b>Naturally, they will catch up in turn,
starting with the fastest runners.</b>

13:03.300 --> 13:07.640
<b>You rely on that fact to look back
and slay one man, then run away again.</b>

13:08.430 --> 13:11.390
<b>If you keep doing that over and over,
you can defeat all the enemies,</b>

13:11.390 --> 13:13.770
<b>or at the very least,
you'll shake them off the trail</b>

13:13.770 --> 13:15.190
<b>and get to safety, that you will.</b>

13:15.190 --> 13:16.350
<b>I see!</b>

13:16.350 --> 13:17.350
<b>But to do that,</b>

13:17.350 --> 13:20.940
<b>you absolutely need the leg power
from heavy training, that you do.</b>

13:21.780 --> 13:23.110
<b>I see.</b>

13:23.360 --> 13:27.160
<b>Basically, how can you bring the situation
around so you can fight one-on-one.</b>

13:27.780 --> 13:30.030
<b>Try thinking about that aspect,
that you should.</b>

13:30.660 --> 13:33.290
<b>A situation
where I can fight one-on-one...</b>

13:34.710 --> 13:35.750
<b>Yahiko.</b>

13:36.620 --> 13:39.170
<b>Kamiya Kasshin-ryu is a life-giving sword.</b>

13:39.170 --> 13:42.670
<b>It is a sword to wield for the sake
of others and a sword to protect people.</b>

13:43.630 --> 13:47.550
<b>You put two destinies, yours and that
of the one you're trying to protect,</b>

13:47.550 --> 13:48.470
<b>on one sword.</b>

13:48.970 --> 13:51.350
<b>If you lose,
not only is it the end for you,</b>

13:51.350 --> 13:53.350
<b>but also for the one
you're trying to protect.</b>

13:53.970 --> 13:57.900
<b>Those that wield life-giving swords
are not allowed defeat of any sort.</b>

13:58.350 --> 14:00.610
<b>Make sure to take that to heart.</b>

14:09.240 --> 14:13.120
<b>AKABEKO OWNER'S HOUSE</b>

14:13.490 --> 14:15.000
<b>All right, let's go!</b>

14:15.200 --> 14:17.870
<b>We really doin' this, Mr. Mikio?</b>

14:17.870 --> 14:21.040
<b>Huh? Why you cowering now after all this?</b>

14:21.540 --> 14:26.470
<b>I told you, merchants' money
is all thanks to samurai to begin with.</b>

14:26.970 --> 14:30.010
<b>It's totally okay
if we take a big chunk of that.</b>

14:30.510 --> 14:32.760
<b>And we aren't gonna fail.</b>

14:32.760 --> 14:35.520
<b>That's why we made this spare key
to begin with—</b>

14:39.690 --> 14:41.230
<b>You're that kid from yesterday!</b>

14:41.520 --> 14:43.230
<b>Damn brat! Give that back!</b>

14:43.520 --> 14:45.610
<b>If you want it, come at me with force!</b>

14:45.610 --> 14:47.360
<b>You're better at that, aren't you?</b>

14:47.490 --> 14:48.700
<b>Damn it, wait!</b>

14:50.450 --> 14:51.780
<b>Little Yahiko.</b>

14:52.830 --> 14:54.870
<b>- Hold it!
- Don't you run!</b>

14:55.080 --> 14:56.330
<b>Now you're cornered.</b>

14:56.330 --> 14:57.580
<b>Resign yourself!</b>

14:59.080 --> 15:02.790
<b><i>The destiny of the one
I'm protecting is on my sword.</i></b>

15:03.500 --> 15:04.960
<b><i>Defeat is not allowed!</i></b>

15:06.210 --> 15:08.590
<b>Kamiya Kasshin-ryu, Yahiko Myojin!</b>

15:08.920 --> 15:11.300
<b>I will fight you fair and square!</b>

15:11.590 --> 15:13.680
<b>You're a rat in a trap! Shut your—</b>

15:15.640 --> 15:17.810
<b>Why are you getting caught, you morons?</b>

15:17.810 --> 15:19.390
<b>Get at him, one at a time!</b>

15:19.390 --> 15:20.350
<b>Huh?</b>

15:25.360 --> 15:26.610
<b>I see.</b>

15:26.980 --> 15:28.690
<b>You pretended
like you were cornered,</b>

15:28.690 --> 15:32.820
<b>but actually were luring us into a place
where you can fight one-on-one.</b>

15:33.030 --> 15:33.870
<b><i>You got me.</i></b>

15:34.370 --> 15:36.540
<b>But that is your fatal error!</b>

15:36.700 --> 15:38.620
<b>He has nowhere to run!</b>

15:38.620 --> 15:40.250
<b>Slowly run him down!</b>

15:40.960 --> 15:42.960
<b>Don't go easy on him!</b>

15:42.960 --> 15:47.550
<b>They'll never catch on to us
killing a guy or two if we bury 'em!</b>

15:50.220 --> 15:51.470
<b>What are you doing?</b>

15:51.800 --> 15:53.550
<b>Hurry up, and move it!</b>

16:02.140 --> 16:03.650
<b>That cross-shaped scar.</b>

16:03.650 --> 16:05.940
<b>That's probably the guy
rumored to be super strong.</b>

16:06.150 --> 16:08.480
<b>The fighter for hire Zanza's here, too!</b>

16:08.480 --> 16:11.150
<b>Run for it!
We're the ones that will be killed!</b>

16:11.150 --> 16:13.240
<b>Hey! Damn it,
why are you guys chickening out?</b>

16:17.540 --> 16:20.750
<b>Well, I guess
that about wraps it up for us.</b>

16:20.750 --> 16:22.250
<b>Guess so, that it does.</b>

16:22.750 --> 16:26.590
<b>But how did you know
that I would come here, that you did?</b>

16:27.090 --> 16:28.750
<b>I left without telling anyone.</b>

16:29.380 --> 16:32.800
<b>I can tell. You said, "Yahiko's battle,"</b>

16:32.800 --> 16:36.390
<b>but his defeat would trouble
that Tsubame girl and Akabeko.</b>

16:36.970 --> 16:39.560
<b>You're not one to leave him alone,
knowing that.</b>

16:40.060 --> 16:42.140
<b>Besides, you're
too ridiculously good-natured</b>

16:42.140 --> 16:46.560
<b>to actually go through with
sending lion cubs down ravines.</b>

16:47.270 --> 16:49.690
<b>I wonder if you're complimenting me
or insulting me.</b>

16:50.480 --> 16:53.450
<b>Well, in any case, from here on...</b>

16:53.650 --> 16:56.950
<b>Yeah. A true one-on-one, that it is.</b>

16:57.490 --> 17:00.830
<b>I didn't think that I
would go against a brat like this</b>

17:00.830 --> 17:05.880
<b>to show the mastery
of the Mikio Nagaoka-ryu!</b>

17:09.670 --> 17:10.500
<b><i>I can see it!</i></b>

17:12.460 --> 17:13.420
<b>Face!</b>

17:16.010 --> 17:19.100
<b><i>I can clearly see
the sword path of a real sword!</i></b>

17:19.680 --> 17:22.930
<b><i>The results of daily training
are really paying off.</i></b>

17:23.980 --> 17:27.560
<b><i>I hate to say it, but I feel grateful
to Kaoru for all of this.</i></b>

17:28.900 --> 17:30.190
<b>Damn brat!</b>

17:32.400 --> 17:36.320
<b>It's dangerous for a girl
to walk alone this late at night.</b>

17:38.240 --> 17:39.370
<b>I'm Kaoru Kamiya.</b>

17:39.870 --> 17:41.790
<b>I'm Yahiko's mentor in swordsmanship.</b>

17:42.410 --> 17:44.250
<b>You came here to stop that guy,
didn't you?</b>

17:47.290 --> 17:51.710
<b>I'm sorry to say it, but, Tsubame,
you won't be able to stop that man.</b>

17:52.510 --> 17:54.340
<b>You can leave Yahiko to take care of this.</b>

17:55.090 --> 17:57.340
<b>But in return,
I'd like you to promise me one thing.</b>

17:57.840 --> 17:59.050
<b>Promise?</b>

17:59.510 --> 18:03.220
<b>If Yahiko wins, you need to feel
more secure about yourself!</b>

18:04.560 --> 18:07.350
<b>Don't be trapped
in a stupid old tradition.</b>

18:07.350 --> 18:10.690
<b>If something like this ever happens again,
you need to clearly say no.</b>

18:11.940 --> 18:15.070
<b>Times have changed, and there is
equality for the four classes.</b>

18:15.070 --> 18:19.160
<b>But if people's hearts don't change,
all of that means absolutely nothing.</b>

18:20.200 --> 18:22.080
<b>Damn little brat!</b>

18:22.080 --> 18:23.830
<b>I've had enough!</b>

18:23.830 --> 18:25.290
<b>Mikio Nagaoka-ryu...</b>

18:25.540 --> 18:28.790
<b>Sure-kill Ukiashi Drop!</b>

18:32.460 --> 18:34.630
<b><i>Damn it, my right foot!</i></b>

18:35.010 --> 18:35.840
<b>Win!</b>

18:36.170 --> 18:38.300
<b>Please win, Yahiko!</b>

18:39.510 --> 18:40.720
<b><i>That's right.</i></b>

18:40.970 --> 18:45.060
<b><i>The destiny of those I protect
is riding on my sword!</i></b>

18:50.400 --> 18:51.810
<b>- Wha—
- Oh!</b>

18:52.770 --> 18:55.280
<b>I'm gonna win!</b>

19:01.070 --> 19:01.910
<b>So...</b>

19:02.910 --> 19:06.120
<b>what the hell are you doing here, Kaoru?</b>

19:06.330 --> 19:07.330
<b>Huh?</b>

19:07.330 --> 19:08.830
<b>Oh, um...</b>

19:09.460 --> 19:12.460
<b>That, and... you two up on the rooftop!</b>

19:17.170 --> 19:18.840
<b>There are no cicadas in springtime!</b>

19:19.550 --> 19:22.760
<b>Sheesh. You guys are such busybodies.</b>

19:24.560 --> 19:28.100
<b>I'll walk Tsubame home,
so you guys can head back without me.</b>

19:28.100 --> 19:30.350
<b>All right. Be careful, that you should.</b>

19:30.850 --> 19:32.860
<b>Thank you so very much, Yahiko.</b>

19:33.360 --> 19:35.110
<b>No need to thank me.</b>

19:35.440 --> 19:39.570
<b>I just hate seeing people
so sobby and jittery.</b>

19:40.070 --> 19:45.280
<b>Yup. So I won't be sobby
or jittery anymore.</b>

19:48.330 --> 19:51.290
<b>Then I'll see you again
tomorrow at Akabeko.</b>

19:52.750 --> 19:55.000
<b>And that settles everything.</b>

19:55.000 --> 19:56.710
<b>No, not yet.</b>

19:57.710 --> 20:01.220
<b>We still haven't heard the reason
why this guy is working!</b>

20:01.720 --> 20:04.600
<b>After all we've been through,
try telling us it's a secret!</b>

20:04.600 --> 20:05.600
<b>When that happens...</b>

20:06.100 --> 20:08.890
<b>All right. I'll say it, okay?</b>

20:09.560 --> 20:11.940
<b>It was so that I can buy a sakabato.</b>

20:11.940 --> 20:15.560
<b>Someday, when I'm as strong as Kenshin,
I want to have one myself.</b>

20:15.560 --> 20:18.400
<b>So I'm just starting
to save up funds for it now.</b>

20:21.990 --> 20:24.240
<b>Y-Yahiko, with a s-sakabato?</b>

20:24.240 --> 20:26.120
<b>Don't laugh about it, bird head!</b>

20:26.120 --> 20:28.120
<b>This is exactly why I kept it a secret!</b>

20:28.290 --> 20:30.660
<b>Listen up! Don't tell Kaoru, okay?</b>

20:30.660 --> 20:32.920
<b>- I'm sure she'd laugh about it, too!
- Sakabato!</b>

20:33.870 --> 20:36.670
<b>- All right, you better not say it!
- But I already heard it.</b>

20:38.840 --> 20:39.710
<b>Kenshin.</b>

20:40.460 --> 20:41.300
<b>Yahiko.</b>

20:42.590 --> 20:44.590
<b>It costs quite a bit, that it does.</b>

20:45.090 --> 20:46.350
<b>It does?</b>

20:46.350 --> 20:47.430
<b>It does, that it does.</b>

20:48.010 --> 20:49.010
<b>So it does.</b>

22:37.000 --> 22:37.830
<b>Okay!</b>

22:45.090 --> 22:50.090
<b>NEXT EPISODE
THAT MAN - RAIJUTA</b>

22:46.260 --> 22:49.590
<b><i>Next episode, "That Man - Raijuta."</i></b>
